ociety&#x02013;USA panel.</article-title><source>Jama</source><volume>296</volume><fpage>827</fpage><lpage>843</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16905788</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001531-Schechter1"><label>30</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schechter</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Treatment at scale in Brazil: a physician's perspective.</article-title><source>Aids</source><volume>21</volume><fpage>S31</fpage><lpage>S35</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17620750</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001531-Instituto1"><label>31</label><citation citation-type="book"><collab>Instituto Brasileiro de Geografia e Estat&#x000ed;stica</collab><year>2006</year><article-title>Proje&#x000e7;&#x000e3;o da Popula&#x000e7;&#x000e3;o.</article-title></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001531-WHO2"><label>32</label><citation citation-type="book"><collab>WHO</collab><year>2007</year><article-title>Health statistics and health information systems.</article-title><publisher-name>WHO</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001531-WHO3"><label>33</label><citation citation-type="book"><collab>WHO</collab><year>2004</year><article-title>International Statistical Classification of Diseases and Health Related Problems ICD-10, Volume 2: Instruction Manual.</article-title><fpage>184</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001531-R1"><label>34</label><citation citation-type="book"><collab>R Development Core Team</collab><year>2006</year><article-title>R: A language and environment for statistical computing. 2.4.0. ed.</article-title><publisher-loc>Vienna, Austria</publisher-loc><publisher-name>R Foundation for Statistical Computing</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001531-Yan1"><label>35</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yan</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><s